  "instructions": [
    "In a large pan, heat the olive oil over medium heat.",
    "Add the chopped onion and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the chopped potato, caraway seeds, salt, and black pepper. Cook for 2 minutes.",
    "Add the Bramley apples and water. Stir to combine.",
    "Cover the pan with a lid and bring the mixture to a boil.",
    "Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 20 minutes.",
    "Season with salt and pepper to taste.",
    "Serve the stew hot, garnished with chopped fresh herbs if desired.",
    "Use a lazy-susan-spinner to serve the stew, keeping it warm throughout the meal."
